rows.en:
...Just as I thought.
Not surprisingly, Iwashita had stayed home from school.
I'd better try someone else.{p}

{f:I|I} whirled around, startled.
The memory of my walk home yesterday had come flooding back{f:.|.}
There was no one behind {f:me|me}.{p}

Kazama had vanished partway through, after finishing his story.
Suddenly, like smoke.
I couldn't believe he had really disappeared for good, so I headed for Kazama's classroom.{p}

"Aaah!"
There stood a giant cockroach...
Yeah, right. There's no way something like that exists{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} pulled off the tasteless mask shaped like a giant cockroach.{p}

Kazama's smirking face emerged from inside the cockroach.
"Ahaha... You're as {f:boring|cute} as ever, you know.
{f:At this rate,|Sorry} {f:you'll never be a hit with the girls like I am.|for scaring you.}
{f:And here I was,|I know!} {f:going to teach you how to get girls.|To make it up to you, I'll take you somewhere nice next time.}"
Talking with this guy always throws me off.{p}

"{f:I know.|Okay?}
{f:As a special favor,|Let's go on a date.} {f:I'll teach you a gag that'll make the girls love you.|I'm sure it'll be fun.}
{f:Right now|Let's see...} {f:it's a special bargain, just five thousand yen.|How about this Sunday?}
{f:So,|Of course,} {f:how about one?|you'll say okay, right?}"{p}

When I went to Fukuzawa's classroom, she was happily chatting with a few other girls.
When {f:I|I} waved, she noticed and waved back.
Then she came trotting over.{p}

"What's up, {c}{f:|}?
Oh, did you just miss me that much?"
"Never mind that, this is serious{f:.|.}
Yesterday {f:we|we} definitely heard Arai's story{f:, right?|, didn't we?}"{p}

When I went to Hosoda's classroom, a few students were still there.
"Um, excuse me, is Hosoda here?"
When {f:I|I} asked no one in particular, they all burst out laughing loudly.{p}

{f:Huh|Whaaat}?
Does Hosoda really like toilets that much{f:?|?}
{f:Oh well|Oh well}.
{f:Guess I'll check the toilets|I'll try looking in the toilets}.{p}

...Hold on, wait a {f:sec|second}.
That's right{f:.|.} When I got home yesterday, for some reason I got a phone call from Hosoda{f:.|.}
I was wondering what it was about when he suddenly started talking about Takeuchi.
Yes, the story of Takeuchi, who never goes to the toilet.
Saying he wanted me to be the only one to hear this, he started telling me something strange{f:.|.}
That the story he told everyone was actually a lie.
That there's no such person as Takeuchi.{p}

{f:Apparently Hosoda had gotten|Hosoda told me he'd gotten} hold of a drink called Sanbura tea abroad, and he drinks it all the time.
Sanbura tea... a tea that, if you drink it, means you never have to go to the toilet again.
He said he'd just told everyone a story he dreamed up while drinking that tea{f:.|.}
He also said some nonsense about letting me have a taste of it as a special treat...
Then why on earth is Hosoda going to the toilet{f:?|?}
Wasn't he supposed to have stopped needing the toilet{f:?|?}
{f:No|No}... maybe he didn't go there to relieve himself.{p}

I hear some people make a daily habit of reading the newspaper on the toilet.
Hosoda must just like the toilet as a place{f:.|.}
And that phone call might have been a joke.
{f:Whoa|Oh}, I don't have time to think about pointless stuff{f:!|.}
I have to find out about Arai...{p}

"Uh, um... Hosoda.
Never mind that, there's something important I need to talk to you about.
Do you remember Arai's doll story?"{p}

I'd try looking for Kiyose.
Then I should be able to tell whether what Hino said was just a joke or the truth{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} headed for Class 3-F, the one Hino had mentioned.{p}

...So Kiyose did exist.
And he hadn't come to yesterday's gathering.
{f:I|I} bowed to Kiyose once more and left Class 3-F.{p}

From what everyone said, {f:sure enough|just as I thought}, Arai had been there at that time, in that place, and told that doll story{f:.|. That's what it all pointed to.}
But Hino hadn't invited Arai.
The one Hino invited was Kiyose, who came down with a fever and couldn't make it.
...What on earth {f:is going on|does this mean}?
Who is Arai, {f:anyway|I wonder}?
Should I find out{f:?|?}{p}Or should I just forget about all this{f:?|?}

Fighting down the chill creeping up my spine, {f:I|I} went around the second-year classrooms one by one.
{f:After all|Because}, after hearing that story, {f:I|I} had seen something eerie that I couldn't explain{f:.|.}
If Arai's story {f:was|was} true, this year's sacrifice might be {f:me|me}.
Why had Arai, who wasn't supposed to exist, come to the newspaper club uninvited and told that story{f:?|?}{p}

"Shindo!"
I turned around, and there stood Shindo.
"{f:You came lookin' for Arai to beat the crap outta him, right|You seen Arai around anywhere}?
{f:Me too.|I'm lookin' for him so I can beat the crap outta him.}"
{f:I hadn't exactly planned to beat him up, but|Shindo} {f:I had come looking for him, just like Shindo.|was scary.}
{f:Somehow,|Besides,} {f:Shindo seemed a little pale.|he seemed a little pale somehow.}{p}

Shindo drew {f:me|me} into the shadow of a pillar.
Then he began to speak in a low voice.
It seemed to be something nobody else should overhear.{p}

...I can't stop thinking about the last thing he said.
One of us is gonna be this year's sacrifice.
And the guy who said that doesn't even exist in this world. Doesn't that creep you out?{p}

If this goes on, the doll will surely never leave {f:my|my} side for even a moment, and it will haunt {f:me|me} to death{f:.|.}
With each new sighting of the doll, I {f:could feel|can feel} {f:myself|myself} losing all will.
I can't shake the feeling that the doll is draining my life force little by little.
I miss the days when I tried to fight the doll, even knowing it was futile resistance{f:.|.}
But doing that {f:is|is} pointless.
The doll can't be touched{f:.|.}
Whenever {f:I|I} try to touch the doll, it vanishes instantly and reappears somewhere else.{p}

Expressionless as it was, it seemed to be sneering at {f:me|me}.
School had long since ended, and summer vacation had begun.
How much longer can {f:I|I} stay alive{f:?|, I wonder?}
Cursing Hino, wishing I'd never taken on that project, is ancient history now{f:.|.}
I don't feel like resenting anyone anymore.
{f:I|I}'d even stopped caring what that being called Arai really was.
Am {f:I|I} just going to die like this{f:?|?}
Should I try relying, just a little, on what scraps of willpower I still have left{f:?|?}{p}
